---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

// The PDF lives at a permanent path (`/cv.pdf`). To publish a new version,
// overwrite public/cv.pdf in place so links already handed out keep working.
// `download` only changes the saved filename, not the URL.
const pdf = `${base}cv.pdf`;
const updated = 'September 2026';
---
<Base
  title="CV — Saki"
  description="Ekow Nii Saki Sackey — software engineer. Backend, cloud and quality assurance."
>
  <article class="prose paper cv">
    <header class="post-head">
      <h1>Ekow Nii Saki Sackey</h1>
      <p class="cv-tagline">Software Engineer · Backend · Cloud · Quality Assurance</p>
      <p class="cv-contact">
        <a href="mailto:ekowsackey22@gmail.com">ekowsackey22@gmail.com</a> ·
        <a href="tel:+233598838503">+233 598 838 503</a> ·
        <span>Accra, Ghana</span>
      </p>
      <p class="cv-contact">
        <a href="https://github.com/ns-ekow" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/ns-ekow</a> ·
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/ns-sackey" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">linkedin.com/in/ns-sackey</a>
      </p>
      <div class="post-links">
        <a class="post-link" href={pdf} download="Ekow-Sackey-CV.pdf">Download PDF ↓</a>
        <a class="post-link" href={pdf} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open PDF ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p class="meta cv-updated">Updated {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <h2>Profile</h2>
    <p>
      Software engineer with a background in Computer Engineering. I have professional Software
      Engineering experience spanning full-stack web development internships and most recently an
      intensive one-year professional training programme in Java, Spring Boot, AWS Architecture and
      Software Quality. I am dedicated and self-driven, a quick learner with strong communication
      skills and an ability to adapt quickly to change. I am technically versatile and willing to
      deepen my expertise while contributing meaningful work to any Software project.
    </p>

    <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
    <dl class="cv-skills">
      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>Java, Python, TypeScript, SQL, Go</dd>

      <dt>Backend</dt>
      <dd>
        Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA, Spring Security, Spring Cloud (Eureka, Gateway), RabbitMQ,
        Resilience4j, REST, GraphQL, Flask, FastAPI, Node.js, Express.js
      </dd>

      <dt>Frontend</dt>
      <dd>Vue 3, Pinia, Vue Router, Vite, React, Next.js, Tailwind CSS</dd>

      <dt>Databases</dt>
      <dd>PostgreSQL, MongoDB, DynamoDB, Redis</dd>

      <dt>Cloud and DevOps</dt>
      <dd>
        AWS (Cloud Practitioner Certified): ECS/Fargate, Lambda, API Gateway, S3, CloudFront, RDS
        and RDS Proxy, DynamoDB, EventBridge, SNS/SQS, Cognito, Amplify, VPC, IAM, CloudFormation,
        SAM; Docker, GitHub Actions, CI/CD, OIDC federation, Infrastructure as Code
      </dd>

      <dt>Testing and Quality</dt>
      <dd>JUnit 5, Vitest, JMeter, VisualVM, test planning, traceability, defect management</dd>

      <dt>AI and ML</dt>
      <dd>RAG pipelines, Hugging Face Transformers, model fine-tuning</dd>

      <dt>Tools</dt>
      <dd>Git, Figma, Postman</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Experience</h2>

    <h3>Software Engineering Trainee (Backend · Cloud · Quality Assurance)</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">AmaliTech, Accra, Ghana · November 2025 - September 2026</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Delivered an internal data validation platform as part of a five-engineer Scrum team:
        volunteered into frontend, then into quality engineering.
      </li>
      <li>
        Served as the project's sole quality gate: raised and drove 58 defects to resolution across
        five epics, reaching handover with no major defects or blockers outstanding.
      </li>
      <li>
        Rebuilt the backend test infrastructure, taking the suite from 296 tests to 445, exercising
        every main path against Testcontainers PostgreSQL, a real SMTP server and a real browser.
      </li>
      <li>
        Authored the product specification after an undocumented mid-project pivot and drove it to
        Product Owner sign-off.
      </li>
      <li>
        Profiled and optimised API performance under load using async patterns, concurrency control
        and caching, with before-and-after measurements taken in VisualVM and JMeter.
      </li>
      <li>
        Delivered multiple AWS-centred lab projects as working deployments within the Cloud
        Computing training curriculum: ECS Fargate with blue/green CI/CD, multi-AZ VPCs in
        CloudFormation, RDS with connection proxying and Redis caching, and event-driven serverless
        on Lambda, DynamoDB and EventBridge.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Full-Stack Developer Intern</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">Mon &amp; Associates, Remote · February 2024 - August 2024</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Transformed AllAcademies, a learning and automated assessment platform, from a bare-bones
        skeleton interface into a polished, intuitive product, owning the full UI/UX redesign end
        to end.
      </li>
      <li>
        Built responsive frontend interfaces using Tailwind CSS and GSAP animations, prototyped in
        Figma ahead of implementation, and contributed to backend development in PHP and Laravel.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Python Development Intern</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">GlobalCode, Accra, Ghana · September 2023 - October 2023</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Went properly into the weeds with Python for the first time across an intensive one-month
        bootcamp, moving from algorithm scripting and data handling into full-stack web development
        with Flask and Bootstrap.
      </li>
      <li>
        Learned to integrate and consume third-party REST APIs, and to reason about how data moves
        between a service, a backend and a rendered page. Gained hands-on experience of the vast
        capabilities of the Python programming language through Raspberry Pi projects.
      </li>
      <li>
        Capstone project: built MEJ News with two other developers as the programme's final team
        deliverable, a news aggregator integrating a third-party news API to fetch, sort and
        categorise articles dynamically, in Flask with a Bootstrap frontend.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Projects</h2>

    <h3>Lab Results Validation App</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">Full-Stack · AmaliTech Internal Platform · June 2026 - September 2026</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Internal platform that ingests instructors' grading workbooks from SharePoint, validates
        them against reference data and maintains a full audit trail. Vue 3 and Pinia frontend
        against a Spring Boot and PostgreSQL backend.
      </li>
      <li>
        Shipped the entire admin and instructor surface as sole frontend engineer: 16 Vue 3 and
        TypeScript screens with role-based access control, plus a design system of tokens and
        primitives.
      </li>
      <li>
        Moved into the sole QA role on the same product and diagnosed its only blocker: change
        detection keyed record identity on a mutable field, so ordinary re-grades were silently
        discarded and same-day duplicates dropped entirely. Traced both failure paths and proposed
        the fix that shipped with a database migration.
      </li>
      <li>
        Made the product testable without its external dependency by refactoring the SharePoint
        integration behind an interface with a fixture-backed implementation, and added a
        17-journey Playwright regression pack.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Food Delivery Platform</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">Microservices · Java, Spring Cloud, RabbitMQ, Docker</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Decomposed a monolithic Spring Boot backend into four independently deployable
        microservices, each with its own database, replacing cross-domain joins with
        service-to-service REST calls.
      </li>
      <li>
        Connected them with Eureka service discovery, a Spring Cloud Gateway handling routing, JWT
        authentication and rate limiting, RabbitMQ event messaging and Resilience4j circuit breakers
        with fallbacks; the full system up and running from a single Docker Compose command.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Serverless Task Manager</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">AWS SAM · Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge, Cognito</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Fully serverless, event-driven application: Cognito authentication, CRUD through API Gateway
        and Lambda onto DynamoDB, and a frontend hosted on Amplify.
      </li>
      <li>
        Implemented per-task scheduled expiry through EventBridge with SNS email notification, and
        idempotent cancellation through DynamoDB Streams into an SQS FIFO queue; defined entirely as
        infrastructure as code with an automated deployment pipeline.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>TwiGPT chatbot</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">Final Year Project · December 2024 - September 2025</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Developed a generative language model based on the GPT architecture, fine-tuned entirely on
        Twi, a low-resource African language; conducted the NLP research under the supervision of a
        Senior Lecturer and built the data collection and training pipelines from the JW corpus and
        transcribed local news sources.
      </li>
      <li>
        Built the serving layer and chat application around it: a single streaming interface hiding
        three different execution paths, namely a local Ollama server, Hugging Face Transformers
        loaded in-process, and a remote Gradio Space.
      </li>
      <li>
        Designed a feedback loop that turned ordinary use of the application into labelled training
        data for the next iteration of the model.
      </li>
      <li>Research thesis graded A.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Education</h2>
    <h3>BSc Computer Engineering</h3>
    <p class="cv-meta">University of Ghana · 2021 - 2025</p>
    <p>Second Class Honours (Upper Division)</p>

    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner, Amazon Web Services</li>
      <li>Generative AI Fundamentals, Databricks</li>
      <li>Responsive Web Design, freeCodeCamp</li>
      <li>Scientific Computing with Python, freeCodeCamp</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Languages</h2>
    <p>English · Ga · Twi</p>

    <div class="post-links post-links--footer">
      <a class="post-link" href={pdf} download="Ekow-Sackey-CV.pdf">Download PDF ↓</a>
    </div>
    <a class="back" href={base}>&larr; Back home</a>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Section headers borrow the mono label treatment used by `section h2`
     elsewhere on the site, which suits a CV's rubric better than prose h2. */
  .cv h2 {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.65;
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent);
  }

  .cv h3 { margin: 1.75rem 0 0; font-size: 1.1rem; }

  .cv-tagline {
    margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  /* Contact lines wrap to their own rows on a phone rather than overflowing. */
  .cv-contact {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.75;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .cv-updated { margin: 1.25rem 0 0; }

  .cv .post-links { margin-top: 1.5rem; }

  /* Org and date line under each role. Not `.meta`, which carries a bottom
     margin sized for a page header. */
  .cv-meta {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    opacity: 0.6;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.6rem;
  }

  /* Label/value grid on wide screens, stacked on narrow. */
  .cv-skills {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, max-content) 1fr;
    gap: 0.45rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.1rem 0;
  }
  .cv-skills dt {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.6;
    padding-top: 0.2rem;
  }
  .cv-skills dd { margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .cv-skills { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.15rem; }
    .cv-skills dd { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  }

  /* Printing the page should yield the CV itself, not the site chrome. */
  @media print {
    .cv .post-links,
    .cv .back { display: none; }
  }
</style>
